hi everyone  so this video aims to provide insight on  how to structure your day and week in  order to get the most out of it  at the moment i'm working on multiple  projects and i identified that  structure and proper evaluation of  psychological and physiological  parameters  is the key to ensuring a productive  schedule without structure  and without understanding your mind and  your body your chances of enjoying a  full and  balanced lifestyle decrease dramatically  and your motivation and your mood suffer  in respect  regardless of how busy you are in your  life the schedule i'll suggest today  will prove  quite helpful i decided to name it the  da vinci schedule because  it is inspired by the legend himself  leonardo da vinci was celebrated  polymath  and he has famously said that just as a  well-filled day brings blessed sleep  so a well-employed life brings a blessed  death  this addict has had a major impact on my  life along with another one from the  great psychiatrist irvin yalum  that reads death anxiety is greater than  those who feel  that they have lived an unfulfilled life  so  in my pursuit of a fulfilled and well  examined life  they both inspired me to keep  re-engineering my schedule  in order to make it more creative  purposeful and fun  the davinci schedule is the result of  this process  the main conundrums that davinci  schedule tries to tackle are  how to be creative and enter flow on a  daily basis  how to not allow interruptions to ruin  your flow  how to stop procrastinating and get  things done  how to make sure you don't experience  burnout  how to make sure you socialize enough  and balance work with play  the main idea behind it is to allow  yourself enough fluidity in your  schedule without getting overwhelmed by  a  profuse amount of tasks here's how it  works  a lot of people suggest that the  planning should start on the first day  of the week  so you can allow yourself some time to  recover from the weekend  in my opinion that is wrong the planning  should start on sunday  evening that is because monday should be  your deep dive day  think of monday as the equivalent of  your early hours in the morning  but for the week in the morning your  mind is rested and it can amaze you with  the productivity it can deliver  your early hours for the week are monday  tuesday  and wednesday in order to take advantage  of that parallel you need to plan your  tasks on sunday  so every sunday evening around seven to  eight pm  sit at your desk reflect on your weekend  focus  and start planning your week from my  point of view this is what your weekly  and daily plan should look like  in rough terms so let me elaborate  firstly we need to use the following  categorization for the daily plan  morning routine deep work admin work  fitness networking and socializing  play  i decided to divide deep work into those  two categories because  deep work is a spectrum that spectrum is  susceptible to its individual's  preferences  for instance i have two activities that  require deep work  writing and video editing due to my  electrical engineering background  i find anything related to technology  quite easy so for me  video editing is easier than writing  therefore video editing is treated as  soft tip work and writing as intensive  work  in essence what this means is that  depending on how you evaluate your deep  work tasks  the intense ones need to be carried out  monday to wednesday  and the soft ones thursday to friday  admin work includes things like email  document organization  ordering supplies scheduling meetings  etc  in short everything that can be done by  a personal assistant but  when you can't afford one you need to  complete yourself these tasks are very  important and oftentimes can take more  time than expected  therefore it is crucial to evaluate via  trial and error the time required to  complete them and plan accordingly  [Music]  when you work in a company meetings are  a crucial element of your schedule  yes they are important and in my  experience they can definitely improve  team building  and project flow but more often than not  they don't add value to your working  flow so my rule for meetings is called  the early late rule what this rule  proposes is that  in order to ensure that a meeting won't  interrupt your deep workflow  meetings need to be scheduled either  early in the morning or late in the  afternoon  that is before 10 am and after 2pm  [Music]  fitness for me includes cardio and  weightlifting or body weight training  i run for two or three miles almost  every morning and i work out at home  three to four times per week running is  incorporated in my morning routine which  i will discuss in a bit  as far as my workout is concerned i like  to work out right after work in order to  avoid late evening fatigue  i make sure to eat something around 4 pm  and i work out around  6 pm in terms of organization workouts  occur  usually monday wednesday and friday and  maybe once during the weekend  i like to keep it like that because it  helps me plan meetups and other events  throughout the week  at least one or two times per week i  like to attend meetups and other  networking events  i consider this important because it  allows me to challenge myself  to socialize to refine my thought  articulation and help me explore  different mindsets and live philosophies  the meetups don't necessarily need to be  business related  they can be philosophy meetups  literature meetups or even  fitness meetups the idea behind this  approach is that  you allow yourself to stay connected  increase your social reach  and also satisfy your need for belonging  this is a time where you can fool around  and indulge in pleasures  these pleasures can vary from reading  and watching youtube videos  to playing video games and going for  drinks with friends  it depends solely on you and your  personal preferences but  my experience has shown that planning  can help you enjoy that process even  more  for instance i like to take some friends  and arrange with them during the week in  advance  or i like to plan a movie on wednesday  evening or i like to schedule a specific  time where i practice some of my hobbies  like  music learning new languages or playing  call of duty  the task list is the most powerful  productivity tool  it really encapsulates the essence of  productivity and helps you declutter  your brain  every day in the morning write down your  five most important tasks and categorize  them effectively  one should include deep work and the  rest should belong to the admin work  domain  flow occurs when you immerse yourself in  uninterrupted deep work  a trick to get there is to listen to  music you enjoy preferably with a beat  that can help brainwaves you know  coordinate and stimulate focus  and shut down all external stimuli like  email  phone and irrelevant browser tabs you  need a good 15 minutes to enter flow and  you can work up to four hours in that  state  therefore i suggest working in that mode  from 10 am  to 2 pm  i have experimented with morning  routines quite extensively and i have  come to the conclusion that  a morning routine can be something very  simple but also  something quite elaborate its goal is to  focus on activities that can galvanize  you motivate you  inspire you help you focus and give you  strength to continue your day fully  energized  for the purposes of this video i will  propose something quite straightforward  but also very effective  so you start your day by waking up  around 6 30  to 7 a.m you run for one or two miles  then you take a cold shower then you  take good care of your skin  if you fast don't eat anything if you  don't fast  cook yourself a big and healthy  breakfast read a book for 30 minutes  read the news or things that interest  you for 20 minutes meditate for 10 to 15  minutes  continue with the rest of your day  at the moment i have to take care of  many projects which means that  i also work during the weekends that  however doesn't mean that i allow myself  to burn out  i consider going out a very healthy  habit and at least once a week i like to  go to a club or a bar  if i go out till late i sleep for at  least eight hours and i wake up  repeating my usual morning routine  then i spend time immersing into  activities that i like  that might include working on projects  surfing  on youtube meeting with friends etc in  any case  your weekend is the time where  everything is allowed and anything you  do  should be stress free  bringing structure to your weekly and  daily schedule is similar to  decluttering your personal space  when you eliminate clutter your mind  perceives your environment  as an organized area that allows it to  analyze patterns in a more effective way  that way you can enjoy an effectual  daily schedule and go to bed  fulfilled just like da vinci so  here is the structure and here's to that  wonderful man leonardo da vinci  may he always be an inspiration to all  of us  hi everyone hope you enjoyed today's  video as always don't forget to like  subscribe  turn on notifications and also let me  know in the comments what is your main  obstacle when it comes  to planning your day and also your week  also i want you to know that i have  written a very detailed ebook and this  is called 30 challenges  30 days zero excuses and it is very  relevant to today's topic  i wrote it initially for me because i  wanted to challenge myself and push  myself  for 30 days to adopt habits evangelized  by the most  influential figures in the personal  development world  in the book i analyze habits like  meditation small talk  power posing journaling sleeping and  many more that can help you enjoy more  productive purposeful  and healthy life it has been read by  thousands of people around the world  and all of them have experienced  significant changes in the way they live  their lives  you can check it out here or the in the  description below  i really suggest you to embark on this  30 day adventure you have nothing to  lose  and so much to gain again thanks for  watching take care  see you soon adrian now  you

